<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<odoo>
    <!--
        BOTH records below are INERT on an upgraded database. Keep them — they
        document the intended state — but do not expect them to do anything.

        `base.group_system` and `base.group_user` are core records whose own
        `ir_model_data.noupdate` is `true`, and `odoo/orm/models.py:5157`
        skips `to_update` when `update and d_noupdate`. The `(3, …)` unlink
        commands are therefore dropped silently on every upgrade: they applied
        once, at install time, and never again. This is the noupdate
        seed-cutover gotcha in its purest form.

        The `base.group_user → health_base.group_healthcare_base` implication
        (`res_groups_implied_rel` row gid=1, hid=346) was authored by an
        earlier version of THIS file, under the comment "Give base users
        healthcare access for debugging", and applied at install on
        2025-12-06. Commit 8be03c5e flipped it to the `(3, …)` unlink below
        and nothing happened, for the reason above.

        What actually removes the row is
        `health_base/migrations/19.0.1.3.8/post-migrate.py` (phase SH-2),
        which also repaired the "Doctor" role mapping that had been
        riding on the defect. Any database still carrying the row converges
        when it upgrades past 19.0.1.3.8. Precedent for hand-deleting a
        DB-only implication row: commit a201b3d1 (356 → 4, so Healthcare:
        Owner no longer granted system admin).
    -->
    <record id="base.group_system" model="res.groups">
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(3, ref('health_base.group_healthcare_owner'))]"/>
    </record>

    <record id="base.group_user" model="res.groups">
        <field name="implied_ids" eval="[(3, ref('health_base.group_healthcare_base'))]"/>
    </record>
</odoo>
